# Everything under docs/spec is a byte-exact snapshot of somebody else's artefact, and several of
# them are wire captures where CRLF is data rather than a line ending. Git's end-of-line
# normalisation rewrites those on commit — with `core.autocrlf=input` set globally it silently
# stripped four bytes out of an `aws-chunked` body here, which the decoder then correctly rejected.
#
# The reason this is worth a file of its own: the corruption happens on the way *into* the
# repository, so the working copy stays valid and the tests stay green for whoever committed them.
# It only appears on a fresh clone — that is, in CI and for every other reader.
#
# `-text` and not `binary`: conversion off, but diffs still readable.
docs/spec/** -text

# The fuzzing corpus is the same kind of thing one layer down: every file is an input somebody's
# parser will read byte for byte, and for the HTTP targets the CRLF **is** the framing. Normalised
# on the way in, a seed stops being the request it was saved as, and a saved crash stops
# reproducing the crash — silently, because the working copy of whoever committed it is fine.
bochka-fuzz/src/test/resources/** -text
